-- A key built from a naming template stored as data, "{parent}-{sequence}",
-- with the sequence zero-padded to three digits. A literal with pieces works;
-- a template held in a field cannot be filled in, a number cannot be padded,
-- and there is no counter.
act Setup { namingTemplate: text }
act Item { setup: one Setup, parentKey: text, sequence: integer
  fromLiteral: text = "${parentKey}-${sequence}" }
-- Wanted, in some spelling: fill(setup.namingTemplate, parent: parentKey,
-- sequence: pad(sequence, 3)), and a sequence the system mints.
